---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../components/IntakeForm.astro';
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';

// Single-page high-converting homepage for KMX Media.
// Designed around the intake form, not portfolio or generic services brochure.
// All copy and structure grounded in "websites that do the work".
// Schema via dedicated component (modeled on reference renderSchema patterns but static + no fakes).
---

<Layout title="KMX Media | Workflow websites, intake systems & AI agents for local businesses">
  <JsonLd slot="head" />

  <!-- Minimal operator nav -->
  <nav class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-white/80 backdrop-blur supports-[backdrop-filter]:bg-white/60">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-5xl items-center justify-between px-5 py-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <div class="h-6 w-6 rounded bg-slate-900"></div>
        <span class="font-semibold tracking-tight">KMX Media</span>
      </div>
      <a href="#intake-form" class="rounded-full border border-slate-300 px-4 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest transition hover:bg-slate-900 hover:text-white">START INTAKE</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <header class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 pb-16 pt-14 md:pt-20">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <div class="inline-block rounded-full bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-600">NOT A BROCHURE SITE. NOT A CMS.</div>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-balance text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tighter text-slate-950 md:text-6xl">
          Websites that do the work.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-600">
          KMX Media builds intake systems, booking and quote flows, structured lead capture, customer follow-up automation, local SEO surfaces, and practical AI workflow agents for local businesses.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="#intake-form" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 px-7 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-sm transition active:scale-[0.985] hover:bg-black">Tell us what your site needs to do</a>
          <a href="#ai-agents" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-2xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 transition hover:border-slate-400">See how AI agents fit operations</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">For operators who need the site to generate calls, bookings, and organized work — not just look good.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <!-- Main intake form (the center of the page) -->
    <section id="intake-form" class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-12 md:py-16">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.1em] text-slate-500">QUALIFIED INTAKE</div>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What should the website actually accomplish?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">Answer the outcome questions first. We design the system around the results you need, not around pages or themes.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-[820px]">
        <IntakeForm />
      </div>

      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-prose text-center text-xs text-slate-500">
        This is version one of the kmxmedia.com intake surface. Form handling is placeholder. See footer and README for exact status.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- AI workflow agents (prominent, practical, grounded) -->
    <section id="ai-agents" class="border-y border-slate-200 bg-white py-12 md:py-16">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5">
        <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-12 md:items-center">
          <div class="md:col-span-5">
            <div class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.1em] text-teal-700">OPERATIONS, NOT THEATRE</div>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">AI agents that handle the busywork</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">We build agents that plug into the workflows your site already runs: intake, follow-up, qualification, and customer communication. They are scoped to concrete tasks so they reduce drag instead of creating new ones.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="md:col-span-7">
            <ul class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-4 text-sm md:grid-cols-2">
              <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-600"></span> Answer repetitive customer questions with accurate, updatable answers</li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-600"></span> Collect missing intake details before a human touches the lead</li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-600"></span> Draft follow-ups and reminders that stay in your voice and policy</li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-600"></span> Route leads to the right person or queue based on answers and availability</li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-600"></span> Prepare quotes or booking requests with the structured data already captured</li>
              <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-600"></span> Keep operational notes, customer context, and content updates organized</li>
              <li class="flex gap-3 md:col-span-2"><span class="mt-1 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-600"></span> Reduce the admin hours spent on the same 20% of conversations and data entry</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-5 text-xs text-slate-500">Agents are always paired with human oversight and clear escalation. They are not a replacement for your judgment or relationships.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Service model / outcome sections -->
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-12 md:py-16">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.1em] text-slate-500">HOW WE ENGAGE</div>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Outcome-driven work, not deliverables</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">We organize projects around what the business actually needs the site (and its connected systems) to produce.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <!-- Card 1 -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
          <div class="text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-500">LAUNCH</div>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Conversion homepage</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">A tight, high-signal homepage whose primary job is turning the right visitors into qualified leads or direct bookings. Strong outcome CTAs and the intake form live here.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">Typical first move for businesses with existing traffic that currently leaks.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 2 -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
          <div class="text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-500">SYSTEM</div>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Booking or quote intake</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Multi-step forms that qualify before you spend time, show relevant options or pricing ranges, capture the structured data you actually need, and produce clean handoff to your team or calendar.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">Replaces email tennis and scattered form responses.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 3 -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
          <div class="text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-500">LOCAL</div>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">GBP traffic → structured leads</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Surfaces and flows that turn Google Business Profile and local search visitors into named, context-rich leads instead of anonymous calls or “send message” black holes.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">The difference between “we get views” and “we get bookable requests”.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 4 -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
          <div class="text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-500">AUTOMATION</div>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">AI agents in the workflow</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Agents scoped to your actual operations: answering FAQs, completing partial intakes, drafting replies, preparing summaries, and keeping the small repetitive things from eating your day.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">Always reviewable. Always under your policies.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 5 -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 md:col-span-2 lg:col-span-1">
          <div class="text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-500">PORTAL (WHEN USEFUL)</div>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Customer-facing pages or self-serve</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">When the business case is clear: simple status views, reschedule or update flows, document collection, or “my requests” grids for repeat customers. Inspired by real customer self-serve patterns but built for your operation, not rides.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">Added only when it removes work for both sides.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Positioning closer -->
    <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-slate-950 py-10 text-slate-200">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 text-center">
        <p class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-sm">
          We are not a creative agency selling websites as content. We are systems builders who make the website (and its connected agents) responsible for moving real work forward for local operators.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 text-[10px] tracking-[0.1em] text-slate-500">KMX MEDIA — NORTHFIELD / TWIN CITIES AREA</div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white py-8 text-xs text-slate-500">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5">
      <div class="flex flex-col justify-between gap-y-3 md:flex-row md:items-center">
        <div>
          © KMX Media. This is the first real version of the kmxmedia.com homepage.
          <span class="block md:inline">Built as a standalone static site (no CMS).</span>
        </div>
        <div class="text-[10px]">
          Form and data handling are placeholder in this version. See README.md in the repo for current status, verification steps, and the exact plan to wire a real endpoint.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
